title: Trouble in Italy
subtitle: The <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> is about to split.
view-if: year == 1922 and month == 10
priority: 2
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: it_psi_seats -= 15; it_psu_seats = 15
tags: event

= <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> split

The 19th <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> Party Congress saw the formal expulsion of the reformist current around Filippo Turati and Giacomo Matteotti which viewed parliamentary cooperation with the Bourgeois as the means to prevent a fascist takeover in Italy. They went on to found their own party called <span style="color: #DD462D;">**PSU**</span> (Unitary Socialist Party).

Meanwhile the Maximalist <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> tried to get to join Comintern which explicitly required the expulsion of said reformists resulting in an earlier split establishing the <span style="color: #88001A;">**PCd'I**</span>. While some (including the Comintern) argue for a formal merger, the <span style="color: #88001A;">**PCd'I**</span> would prefer individual memmbers to join as some Maximalists seem to attempt a Ledebourist course and become the Italian <span style="color: [+ uspd_colour +];">**USPD**</span>...

- @succesful_merger: The <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> will merge with the <span style="color: #88001A;">**PCd'I**</span>.
- @historical_shit: No arrangment can be made.


@succesful_merger
view-if: kpd_relation >= 85 and uspd_relation >= 70
subtitle: Our succesful inter-left cooperation inspired the Italian Socialists.
on-arrival: it_psi_seats += it_pci_seats; it_pci_seats = 0; strong_communism_italy = 1

While some <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> members are sceptical of the merger it seems most important to fight fascism by all means.

- @alignment_italy

@historical_shit

As it seems the Socialist movement in Italy has split in three now, with no current clearly on top. Let's just hope they will stop Mussolini somehow...

- @alignment_italy

@alignment_italy
title: The left has more parties than members...

Who should we align ourselves with now?

- @psu: The reformist <span style="color: #DD462D;">**PSU**</span>
- @psi: The maximalist <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span>
- @psi_left: The radical <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span>
- @psu_and_psi: The <span style="color: #DD462D;">**PSU**</span> and the <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span>
- @psu_and_psi_left: The <span style="color: #DD462D;">**PSU**</span> and the <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span>
- @psi_and_pci: The <span style="color: #E02051;">**PSI**</span> and the <span style="color: #88001A;">**PCd'I**</span>
- @all_of_them: We will support all the Italian Workers' Parties in their struggle against Fascism.


@psu
choose-if: (reformist_strength >= 25 and left_strength <= 20) or labor_strength >= 40
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSU"
unavailable-subtitle: The reformist faction lacks the influence to convince the party of this.


@psi
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 0
choose-if: (center_strength + left_strength) > reformist_strength
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSI"
unavailable-subtitle: The reformist faction doesn't want to support the PSI.

@psi_left
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 1
choose-if: left_strength >= 50
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSI"; comintern_relation += 2
unavailable-subtitle: Our left wing lacks the influence to convince the party of this.

@psu_and_psi
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 0
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSU and PSI"

@psu_and_psi_left
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 1
choose-if: (center_strength + left_strength) > reformist_strength
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSU and PSI"
unavailable-subtitle: The reformist faction doesn't want to support the PSI.

@psi_and_pci
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 0
choose-if: left_strength >= 87
on-arrival: italian_ally = "PSI and PCd'I"; comintern_relation += 3
unavailable-subtitle: Our left wing lacks the influence to convince the party of this.

@all_of_them
view-if: strong_communism_italy == 0
choose-if: (center_strength >= 75 or labor_strength >= 80) and reformist_strength < 30 and left_strength < 30
on-arrival: italian_ally = "The working class"; comintern_relation += 1
unavailable-subtitle: This position is too centrist for our party... (Kautsky would be proud though)















